# The console's configuration. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you need.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With none of it set the app runs against the
# local Workers through the dev proxy and never mentions LumioGuard.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where each tool's Worker answers, one per tool, named from the tool's id.
#
# Leave unset in development: `pnpm dev` proxies `/<tool>/api` to that tool's
# Worker on the port ports.json gives it. Production needs one per tool, and a
# tool with none set will fail its reading rather than guess an origin.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_SLOPMETER_API_URL=https://lumioguard-slopmeter-api.<subdomain>.workers.dev
# VITE_LEAKPEEK_API_URL=https://lumioguard-leakpeek-api.<subdomain>.workers.dev
# VITE_CITECHECK_API_URL=https://lumioguard-citecheck-api.<subdomain>.workers.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The LumioGuard hand-off. One flag governs every mention of it: the button and
# its offer, the wordmark on the masthead, and the credit in the colophon.
#
# Unset means the integration is OFF and the app never says the name. There is
# no address baked in to fall back to, deliberately: a fork must not advertise
# something it does not have.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_LUMIOGUARD_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
#
# Where the WORDMARK points, as distinct from where the hand-off button goes.
# The button carries a reading into the app; the name in the masthead and the
# colophon is a credit and belongs on the page that says what LumioGuard is.
# Falls back to the app URL when unset.
# VITE_LUMIOGUARD_SITE_URL=https://lumioguard.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where this deployment answers, as a bare origin with no path.
#
# The canonical, the OpenGraph URL, the structured data, sitemap.xml and the
# `Sitemap:` line in robots.txt are all absolute by definition, so none of them
# can be written without this. UNSET means every one of them is omitted and the
# build says so on stderr.
#
# There is no address baked in to fall back to, for the same reason the hand-off
# has none: a fork that deployed this would otherwise ship a canonical pointing
# at somebody else's host, which is `document.foreign-canonical`, a blocker in
# the tool this app ships.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://lumioguard-readout.pages.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics, which is OFF unless a key is set. Nothing is loaded and no request
# is made without one, so a fork ships a console that calls nobody.
#
# Configured to match `assets/consent.js` on the marketing site exactly: capture
# starts cookielessly and an accepted cookie banner upgrades it, so the two
# halves of one site never count differently. The choice is read from the
# `lg-consent` key that banner writes, which only reaches here when both are
# served from the same origin.
#
# VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL above is also the guard: analytics counts nothing at any
# other origin, which is what keeps localhost and preview deploys out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
#
# A first-party reverse proxy for PostHog. Its own host when unset.
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://p.lumioguard.dev
#
# Only needed behind that proxy, where toolbar and dashboard links still need
# the real UI host.
# VITE_POSTHOG_UI_HOST=https://us.posthog.com
